      "heading": "C Knowledge Dossier",
      "learner_facing": true,
      "markdown": "# C — Knowledge Dossier\n\nFACT_ID: C-F01 | anchor: A01\nFlex lanes use overhead green arrow to permit and red X to prohibit [A01]\nSource: [A01 -> src:rdmv-ut-class-d:utah-dld:handbook:pdf-0049]\n\nFACT_ID: C-F02 | anchor: A01\nFreeway keeps following gap and bans U-turns and emergency-lane travel [A01]\nSource: [A01 -> src:rdmv-ut-class-d:utah-dld:handbook:pdf-0049]\n\nFACT_ID: C-F03 | anchor: A02\nExpress lane needs 2 or more occupants and bans crossing double white [A02]\nSource: [A02 -> src:rdmv-ut-class-d:utah-dld:handbook:pdf-0050]\n\nFACT_ID: C-F04 | anchor: A02\nC-decal single-occupant clean-fuel use needs one-time 10 fee sticker [A02]\nSource: [A02 -> src:rdmv-ut-class-d:utah-dld:handbook:pdf-0050]\n\nFACT_ID: C-F05 | anchor: A03\nEnter by acceleration lane and exit by early move plus ramp meter stop [A03]\nSource: [A03 -> src:rdmv-ut-class-d:utah-dld:handbook:pdf-0051]\n\nFACT_ID: C-F06 | anchor: A03\nRunaway ramp bans non-emergency use and SPUI U-turn needs green arrow [A03]\nSource: [A03 -> src:rdmv-ut-class-d:utah-dld:handbook:pdf-0051]\n\nFACT_ID: C-F07 | anchor: A04\nIntersection scans controls and stops behind line and keeps gap [A04]\nSource: [A04 -> src:rdmv-ut-class-d:utah-dld:handbook:pdf-0052]\n\nFACT_ID: C-F08 | anchor: A05\nContinuous flow left uses offset crossover and right obeys posted signs [A05]\nSource: [A05 -> src:rdmv-ut-class-d:utah-dld:handbook:pdf-0053]\n\nFACT_ID: C-F09 | anchor: A06\nYellow divides opposite flows and white divides same flow plus 500 limit [A06]\nSource: [A06 -> src:rdmv-ut-class-d:utah-dld:handbook:pdf-0054]\n\nFACT_ID: C-F10 | anchor: A07\nBasic law is reasonable and prudent with 20 and 25 and 55 zones [A07]\nSource: [A07 -> src:rdmv-ut-class-d:utah-dld:handbook:pdf-0055]\n\nFACT_ID: C-F11 | anchor: A08\nRoundabout yields on entry and signals use red yellow green order [A08]\nSource: [A08 -> src:rdmv-ut-class-d:utah-dld:handbook:pdf-0056]\n\nDomains covered: flex freeway express intersections markings speed signals signs right-of-way\nPassing standard exact: stated in Section A\nHigh-yield ranked: signals intersections speed markings right-of-way\nMisconceptions: left-lane camping is allowed; crossing double white is allowed\nMnemonics: RGX for red X bans; YIELD courtesy list\nGlossary: flex lane; express lane; ramp meter; diverging diamond; shared center lane\nDynamic facts isolated: express toll rates and C-decal eligibility lists change; see updatable note\nCompetitive teardown: pending scout; typed debt in E2\nMarket pack: typed debt in E; no invented demand\nAccuracy sourced: each fact block carries its anchor and source trailer\nVerify list consolidated: see Section F",
